      "content": "thanks for that. i guess my question is, do you think those legal theories actually hold up? like, some people say the \"no harm\" argument is a bit of a stretch because the economic benefits of slavery were passed down through generations, so there is a direct link. is there any serious scholarly weight to the idea that the legal/philosophical arguments for the opposition are actually strong, or are they mostly just used to stall progress?",
